+## Control ground (`--control-ground`)
+
+A directory source may declare that its directory is **Control ground**:
+`source add-directory <id> <dir> --control-ground`. Central (the sibling
+product) authors machine and personal skills on Control ground
+(`Control/user/skills/`, `Control/machines/<machine>/skills/`) and project
+skills on ProjectCentral ground (`<project>/ProjectCentral/user/skills/`),
+publishing each skill's standing beside its `SKILL.md` in a `skill.json`
+manifest — the `central.skill/v1` contract.
+
+AIKit reads exactly that published contract and nothing beyond it, the same way
+the harness adapters read Central projections: no path heuristics, no inferred
+semantics. At `sync`, a skill directory carrying a valid `skill.json` contributes
+its standing, scope and provenance to the capsule as `[metadata.control]`
+capability metadata; a skill without one stays an ordinary skill, so existing
+sources are unaffected. A contract violation — an unknown schema, an
+unresolvable standing, a retirement without who/when/why, a manifest name that
+disagrees with the directory — refuses the sync naming the file rather than
+guessing. A source that did not opt in never opens `skill.json` at all.
+
+One value has teeth: **a retired standing never projects.** Projection is
+inclusion, so retirement extends what is withheld rather than building a second
+catalogue — the retired skill remains a member of its sets, and `aikit set show`
+discloses it as withheld with the owner's own retirement reason from the ground
+manifest (never as missing, never as an error). The resolver holds this opinion:
+`RetiredStanding` outranks every other availability gate. Because the standing
+is read at sync time, a standing change on the ground is picked up by the normal
+`sync` → `promote` cycle; it always produces a new snapshot digest.
+
+Project scopes register the same way. Whether a ProjectCentral-ground skill
+projects is decided by the enable scoping and Project Specifications that
+already exist — bound inside the project root, absent outside it — with no new
+routing mechanism.
+
 ## Composition and project binding
 
 Skill Sets are reusable named projections over source-qualified skill ids.
